{
  "about": "Drives and roads shared by the Kotlin and Swift speeding checks. Positions are metres east (x) and north (y) of origin, turned into degrees with lat = origin.latitude + y / 111320 and lon = origin.longitude + x / (111320 * cos(origin.latitude)); road points are then rounded to 1e-5 degrees. Each case starts at `start` at startTime. A move step adds count fixes, one every `every` seconds (default 1): time goes up by every seconds, the position moves speed * every metres along `heading` (degrees clockwise from north, default 90), and the fix reports speed. A pause step adds seconds without fixes. Every fix has 5 m accuracy. Limits are tenths of km/h with source 0 unknown, 1 posted, 2 road type. noPack means no Speed limit pack covers the drive. Expected events are in record order: offset and duration in seconds, peak in m/s within 0.01, limit as tenths of km/h and source. Mph speeds: 29 = 12.964, 34 = 15.1994, 35 = 15.6464, 40 = 17.8816, 50 = 22.352, 70 = 31.2928, 78 = 34.8691, 79 = 35.3162.",
